reports.blockerText:
- Retest on current main. The waterfall planning in #5089 merged and was then reverted (#5824), so main again needs #757/#758 and the local per-lane changes for the waterfall image read below.
- Memory: preparing all the shaders at registration held 16.5 GB of private memory without the memory changes listed at the end. #5181 (plans keep only evaluable branch conditions) covers most of it. After that, the biggest owners are texture uploads (about 3.8 GB, capped with `APS5_TEXTURE_CACHE_MIB`) and the dispatch cache (about 2.5 GB).
- Boot time (about 3 minutes of black screen with a warm cache): in a profile of the boot, the game's loader threads spent about 80% of their time waiting on the process-wide registration lock (#2292). #5023 works in this area.
- Menu speed (about 3.8 FPS): not profiled yet on this title. #1201 and #1747 work on the single queue worker.
- Unproposed stops, each passed locally with an experiment:
  - domain programs that read the ring at a control point computed from data (the domain counterpart of #4727);
  - two-sample rasterization into one-sample color targets, for the checkerboard rendering (approximated locally by drawing the first sample). simonbronk mentions a mixed-samples approach in #5169;
  - wave32 compute programs whose `v_movreld` window hid descriptor dwords (six programs);
  - `guest snapshot differs from registered memory` for image-table records. `APS5_NO_SNAPSHOT_CHECK=1` also passes it; locally the dispatch is recaptured instead.
